    <GaugingStation location="Ness" name="Rye" number="27049">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Flat-V weir on the River Ness in a rural catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Flat V weir subject to drowning below QMED, some out of bank flow but no by-passing. Theoretical rating amended by hydraulic modelling to cover non-modular flow range. One peak flow rating across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat-V weir, 12m wide. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">June 2005 peak estimated at 75 cumecs using hydraulic model.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Significant groundwater abstractions.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Geology: Jurassic Limestone, clays and sandstones. Predominantly rural catchment with moorland headwaters and arable in lower valleys.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GN</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Well gauged to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged close to AMAX1 and high flow rating supported by hydraulic modelling." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
